  "name": "Assessment of Pelagic and Nearshore Fish in Three Bays on the East and South Coasts of Kodiak Island.",
  "description": "This report references geographic distribution and species composition data of fish species (Ammodytes hexapterus); morphometrics data of fish species (Anoplarchus purpurescans), species composition data of fish species: Anoplarchus purpurescans, Clupea pallasi, Hexagrammos decagrammus, Hexagrammos lagocephalus, Hexagrammos octogrammus, Hexagrammos stelleri, and Pholis laeta; and salinity and temperature data of water from Alitak Bay, Kaiugnak Bay, Ugak Bay, Kodiak Island, Alaska. The aforementioned data are referenced in citation: Harris, C. K. and A. C. Hartt. 1977. Assessment of pelagic and nearshore fish in three bays on the east and south coasts of Kodiak Island. University of Washington Fish Res. Inst. Final Report. This literature was collected as part of a metadatabase that represents one or more nearshore resources (from physical attributes such as water and air, to birds and mammals). Each entry is viewable in three formats, 1) a geospatial explicit format (ArcView 3.3) named GIS ArcView 3.3 Near GEM project, 2) a spreadsheet format (Excel 2002 and within ArcView) named GEM Nearshore Metadata Set, and 3) a ProCite database named GEM Nearshore Metadata References, which consists of references included in 1 and 2 above. The ProCite database record number corresponds to the Excel Procite Number. Reference Procite #417 for this literature's metadata. The metadata are maintained in digital format (ArcView 3.3, Excel 2002, and Procite) and are available from the Alaska Science Center, USGS in Anchorage, Alaska. For a detailed description of the three databases and the project, see \"Bodkin, J. L., and T. Dean. 2003. Alternative Sampling Designs for Nearshore Monitoring (Gulf Ecosystem Monitoring and Research Project G-030687), US Geological Survey, Alaska Science Center, Anchorage, Alaska.\" available on-line at http://www.evostc.state.ak.us/pdf/GEM_final_reports/030687.pdf.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Part of the design effort of the \"Alternative Sampling Designs for Nearshore Monitoring\" (Gulf Ecosystem Monitoring and Research Project). Provides a comprehensive historical perspective of locations and types of past studies conducted in the nearshore marine communities within Gulf of Alaska in the form of a geographical information system database.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23571578",
